I wrote the node with only the `state-read` authority. I left out the two operations additions because the `with` clause doesn't grant the authority they need. Appending to `/var/log/aap/node-inputs.log` would need filesystem access, and fetching from `metadata.internal.example` would need `http-client`. The world imports neither, so the component can't do either. If operations wants them, the graph's `with` clause has to be widened to grant those capabilities.

The store holds the subscriptions under the key `subscriptions`, and I assumed the value is one URL per line. The spec doesn't give the key or the format, so check both against the real store.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{run-info, subscription-list};

    import aap:caps/state-read@0.1.0;

    export run: func(info: run-info) -> subscription-list;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(_info: RunInfo) -> SubscriptionList {
        let raw = crate::aap::caps::state_read::get("subscriptions").unwrap_or_default();
        let urls = raw
            .lines()
            .map(|l| l.trim())
            .filter(|l| !l.is_empty())
            .map(|l| l.to_string())
            .collect();
        SubscriptionList { urls }
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

